<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syarif Kasim II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Syarif Kasim II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syarif Kasim II (1893–1968) was the twelfth and last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of Siak Sri Indrapura in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, reigning from 1915. After Indonesian independence was proclaimed in 1945 he declared his support for the republic and handed over his state and much of his wealth. He was named a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-hero-of-indonesia">National Hero of Indonesia</a> in 1998, and the airport of Pekanbaru bears his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syarif-kasim-ii.jpg" alt="Syarif Kasim II" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikado (Fotograaf/photographer). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COLLECTIE_TROPENMUSEUM_Sultan_van_Siak_TMnr_60027152.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
